The sensor's third mode, 1280x720, that had not been ported

The vendor file carries THREE modes and only two had been ported. The one that
was missing is the gentlest of the three on the link:

    5184x3880   op_pre=3 mult=140 0x0312=0   ->  896 MHz
    2592x1940   op_pre=3 mult=187 0x0312=2   -> 1196,8 MHz
    1280x720    op_pre=2 mult=125 0x0312=2   -> 1200 MHz, with a fifth of the
                                                pixels and of the lines

It is put first while investigating why no image arrives: it is the operating
point that asks the least of the receiver, and trying a different point is one
of the few things left unmeasured after having contrasted the sensor, the
CSIPHY and the CSID register by register against the phone's own Android kernel.

The table comes out of the vendor blob with the same reader and the same format
as the other two: addresses in u64[2::10] of the regSetting, values in the
registerData that follow. The other two are verified against the vendor (66 of
66 the mode one, 244 of 244 the initialisation one read back from the sensor's
RAM).
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
@@ -616,9 +616,107 @@
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x6f12), 0x38c8 },
 };
 
